"{{Term/Store|EX Treasure: Usurper King||Series, BotW}}" is a [[Side Quest]] in {{BotW}}.<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|EX Treasure: Usurper King}}<br/>{{Color BotW|Side Quest|Deya Village Ruins}}|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref> It is exclusive to {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack.

==Overview==
This [[Side Quest]] is obtained upon leaving the [[Great Plateau]] and loading the overworld of [[Hyrule Kingdom]], which can be done by [[Warping]], reloading a save file, dying, or leaving an [[Ancient Shrine]]. When the Quest is activated, [[Link]] will be tasked with finding ''[[Misko's EX Journal 2]]'', which is rumored to be in the [[Deya Village Ruins]].<ref>{{Cite|Somewhere in the {{Color BotW|Red|Deya Village Ruins}} is a journal that places the location of this treasure...|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>{{Note|It is possible to activate the second stage of this Side Quest by reading ''Misko's EX Journal 2'' without triggering any of the loading conditions for its activation.}}

Within ''Misko's EX Journal 2'' are clues to the locations of six [[Treasure Chest]]s, each containing a priceless relic stolen from [[Hyrule Castle]] by [[Misko]].<ref>{{Cite|I hid the six priceless relics I stole from Hyrule Castle in treasure chests... I shall write down their locations. -{{Color BotW|Blue|Misko}}|Misko's EX Journal 2|BotW}}</ref> The Journal states the helmet of the self-proclaimed [[Zant|King of Shadows]] can be found in the mire of a valley of dead trees, south of [[Dueling Peaks]].<ref>{{Cite|The helm of the self-proclaimed King of Shadows is {{Color BotW|Red|in the swamp of the valley of dead trees, south of Dueling Peaks}}.|Misko's EX Journal 2|BotW}}</ref>

The Treasure Chest can be found buried between two dead trees on a small island in [[Tobio's Hollow]]. Using the [[Magnesis]] [[Rune]], Link can pull it out of the ground and open it. The Side Quest is completed once Link obtains [[Zant's Helmet]].<ref>{{Cite|You found the treasure that was hidden at Tobio's Hollow and obtained {{Color BotW|Red|Zant's Helmet}}!|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

